{"name":"Vanilla","hex":"#f3e5ab","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vanilla","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Orchidaceae – the vanilla orchid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vanilla"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vanilla","blocks":[{"text":"Vanilla is a spice derived from orchids of the genus Vanilla, primarily obtained from the seed pods of the flat-leaved Mexican and Central American vanilla (V. planifolia)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_%286998639597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla","wikidata":"Q13241"},{"title":"Vanilla (genus)","blocks":[{"text":"Vanilla orchids form the flowering plant genus Vanilla made of about 110 species in the orchid family (Orchidaceae). These orchids are found in tropical and subtropical regions worldwide, from tropical America to tropical Asia, New Guinea and West Africa. Five species are known from the contiguous United States, all limited to southern Florida."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Vanillebl%C3%BCte1.jpg/330px-Vanillebl%C3%BCte1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla_(genus)","wikidata":"Q162044"},{"title":"Vanilla (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color vanilla is a rich tint of off-white as well as a medium pale tint of yellow."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Vanilla_planifolia_1.jpg/330px-Vanilla_planifolia_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanilla_(color)","wikidata":"Q7914921"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vanilla_6beans.JPG/500px-Vanilla_6beans.JPG?utm_source=en.wik